artifact.self_contained_problem:
Consider a federated learning system in which a central server coordinates training of a global model with parameters $\theta \in \mathbb{R}^d$ over $T$ rounds, by aggregating updates from a population of $N$ clients. In round $t$, the server selects a subset $S_t \subseteq \{1,\dots,N\}$ of clients with $|S_t| = m \ll N$, broadcasts the current model $\theta_t$, and each client $i \in S_t$ either (a) returns a model update $\Delta_i^t$ computed from its local dataset $D_i$ (model-update poisoning capability), or (b) supplies corrupted local training data $\tilde D_i$ used in computing an otherwise honest update (data poisoning capability). The server aggregates via some rule $A$ to produce $\theta_{t+1} = A(\{\Delta_i^t\}_{i \in S_t})$.

Define an adversary by a tuple of capabilities $\mathcal{C} = (B, K, T_a, V, P, M)$ where:
(i) $B \subseteq \{1,\dots,N\}$ is a set of Byzantine clients controlled by the adversary, possibly colluding (i.e., coordinating their messages with full knowledge of one another);
(ii) $K \in \{\text{data-poisoning},\text{model-update-poisoning}\}$ specifies the adversary's access level;
(iii) $T_a \in \{\text{untargeted},\text{targeted-backdoor}\}$ specifies the attack objective, where a targeted backdoor is a function $b: \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{X}$ and target label $y^*$ such that the adversary seeks $f_\theta(b(x)) = y^*$ for inputs $x$ in a trigger distribution while preserving accuracy on clean data;
(iv) $V \in \{\text{black-box},\text{white-box}\}$ specifies whether the adversary knows the server's aggregation rule, defenses, and current model;
(v) $P \in [0,1]$ bounds the per-round participation rate of compromised clients ($\mathbb{E}[|B \cap S_t|]/m \le P$);
(vi) $M$ is an evasion-time capability allowing modification of test inputs within a perturbation set $\mathcal{B}(x)$.

A defense is a pair $(A, R)$ where $A$ is a robust aggregation rule and $R$ is an optional auxiliary detection or filtering mechanism.

Problem: Formulate a rigorous evaluation framework — including precise threat models, success metrics, and benchmark protocols — that allows one to assess any proposed defense $(A,R)$ against the full space of adversary capability tuples $\mathcal{C}$ above. In particular, design provable guarantees or empirical methodology that:
(1) distinguish defenses effective under data-poisoning only from those effective under unrestricted model-update poisoning;
(2) account for collusion among Byzantine clients with white-box access;
(3) handle targeted backdoor attacks where the backdoor trigger is unknown to the defender at evaluation time;
(4) incorporate the limited and possibly biased participation pattern of compromised clients across rounds;
(5) jointly evaluate training-time poisoning and inference-time evasion under a unified adversary.

Provide either a defense $(A,R)$ with proven robustness across this taxonomy, or impossibility results delineating which combinations of capabilities $\mathcal{C}$ admit no defense achieving bounded degradation of the global model's accuracy and backdoor success rate.

